  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatClin3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "Today, you\u2019re meeting with a research team to learn more about
    a clinical trial. However, before you can officially decide whether to participate
    in the trial, there\u2019s one very important step that every patient must go
    through first.\r\n\r\n<b>As a patient, what should you always receive before
    joining a clinical trial?</b>\r\n"
  explanation: "Before joining a clinical trial, patients must receive and review
    an informed consent form. This form explains the purpose of the study, possible
    risks and benefits, and the patient\u2019s rights as a participant, including
    the right to leave the trial at any time. Importantly, it\u2019s not a contract
    \u2013 signing doesn\u2019t lock you in. Instead, it\u2019s there to protect
    you and give you the information you need to decide what\u2019s best for you."
  correctAnswer: "An informed consent form explaining the risks, benefits, and participant\u2019s
    rights"
  incorrectAnswer1: A study participation contract with information about the research
    team
  incorrectAnswer2: An informational video about the new treatment being studied
  incorrectAnswer3: A free t-shirt from the research team
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Clinical
